{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Though</b> — Though a camp encamp upon me, meaning they are from the nations, and even if they are many, and even if I need to come to war against them — <b>in this</b>, and the meaning is: that HaShem is my light and my salvation." "And some say: <b>in this</b> — it is the request mentioned afterward."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:39.597546544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}